-- title:
--   Crossing presentation at a supersingular node for q<5
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an integer $N\ge 1$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $red\colon A\to k$; fix modular polynomial data `data` at $q$ (a monic $\Phi\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ with $\Phi(j,j_q)=0$) satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi\equiv(Y^{q}-X)(Y-X^{q})\bmod q$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q\nmid N$ and $q<5$; that $R$ `IsModel`, i.e. the two divisor laws at places not fixed by the square of the geometric Frobenius and the two cusp laws hold; and that $R$ satisfies `OrderLawFixed`: for $f$ integral for both prolongations with nonzero residues and $D$ the divisor of $f$, at every affine place $v$ of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` fixed by the square of `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel` the push-forward of $D$ along `reduceFst` at $v$ equals $\mathrm{ord}_v(\mathrm{residue}_1 f)+\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{Frob}\,v}(\mathrm{residue}_2 f)$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places, all supersingular (rational, affine, with $j$-value in `ssJSet q k`), for which $R$ satisfies `RegularityLaw W` and `NodeValueLaw W`. Let $K\subseteq\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a number field and $w\in W$. Write $\mathcal{O}=A\cap K$ (`NodeLocalized.coeffSubring`) and let $B=R.\mathtt{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ be the ring of elements of the function field at level $Nq$ integral for both prolongations and for every place above $w$ under `reduceFst`, whose expansion lies in the field generated by the constants of $K$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$. Assume both residue maps are saturated on $B$: whenever $g,g'\in B$ with $\mathrm{ord}_w$ of the first residue of $g$ positive and that of $g'$ equal to $1$, the first residue of $g$ is the first residue of $g'$ times that of some $b\in B$, and likewise for the second residue with respect to the place $\mathtt{arithFrobC}\,q\,k\,N\cdot w$. Finally let $c_0$ be node coordinates over $K$ at $w$ (a pair $x_0,y_0\in B$ with first residue of $x_0$ zero, second residue of $x_0$ of order $1$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, second residue of $y_0$ zero, first residue of $y_0$ of order $1$ at $w$) and let $\varpi\in\mathcal{O}$ be such that an element of $\mathcal{O}$ has zero reduction under $red$ exactly when it is a multiple of $\varpi$. Then there exist node coordinates $c=(x,y)$ over $K$ at $w$ with $(\varpi,x)=(\varpi,x_0)$ and $(\varpi,y)=(\varpi,y_0)$ as ideals of $B$ (constants being taken via `nodeConst`), an integer $e_K\ge 1$ and a unit $\varepsilon\in\mathcal{O}$ with $q=\varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$, and an integer $E\ge 1$ and a unit $u\in B$ with $xy=\varpi^{E}u$, such that $(\varpi,x,y)$ is maximal and is the only maximal ideal of $B$, the ideals $(\varpi,x)$ and $(\varpi,y)$ are prime, and $y\notin(\varpi,x)$, $x\notin(\varpi,y)$.
--
--   This is the normal form of an ordinary double point (two smooth branches crossing, with crossing exponent $E$) for the local ring of the reduction of $X_0(Nq)$ at a supersingular node, in the wild residue characteristics $q=2$ and $q=3$ permitted by the hypothesis $q<5$. It is the small-characteristic half of the corresponding statement with no restriction on $q$, which cites it alongside the case $q\ge 5$.
